  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've uploaded several avatars over the years of playing VRChat. As some of these avatars are 4-5+ years old, some of them are broken, some are out-of-date and unused, etc.\n\nHowever, the only method of deletion is through the VRChat Website or the SDK. When I'm scrolling through my avatars in-game and I come across one that has broken, I'd need to either open Unity or use the VRChat website to remove it, both of which can be either tedious or even difficult for other users.\n\nAdding this would assist Users in being able to delete their old avatars immediately when they find one that may have broken due to an update, enabling them to reduce clutter not just in their menu, but on the VRChat servers themselves, without forcing them to need to get out of the headset to browse the website or open Unity.",
